      "writtenOn": "2026-11-11T08:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If check_resp_room() fails here, we unlock slot_lock without setting sess_slot-\u003ein_use \u003d true and drop the session ref, but data-\u003ecd_slot and data-\u003esa_cachethis are already set:\n\n- complete_nfs4_compound() will then write to data-\u003ecd_slot without a session ref (same UAF as https://review.gerrithub.io/c/ffilz/nfs-ganesha/+/1259048 if the session is destroyed concurrently) and with in_use \u003d\u003d false (so it can race with another request on the same slot).\n- Since the comment here says we do want to cache the failed response, maybe we should set sess_slot-\u003ein_use \u003d true and unlock slot_lock before check_resp_room(), and not drop the session ref in this error path so compound_data_Free() cleans up both in_use and data-\u003esession after complete_nfs4_compound()?",
